blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the REBAR_ROOT cut with repo_root()'s real precedence (explicit>REBAR_ROOT>git-toplevel>cwd): either add a resolver that preserves completion_banking's explicit>REBAR_ROOT>cwd (no git-toplevel) behavior, or state and justify the fingerprint delta from adopting repo_root().","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.1,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["completion_banking.py L447-451: `if repo_root: base=Path(repo_root) else: env_root=os.environ.get('REBAR_ROOT'); base=Path(env_root) if env_root else Path.cwd()`","_config_sources.repo_root docstring L33: 'Order: explicit arg > REBAR_ROOT > git toplevel of cwd' (then Path.cwd() fallback)","Plan Outcome requires 'operation-snapshot fingerprints unchanged except deltas recorded'"],"finding":"The plan proposes routing the REBAR_ROOT read in completion_banking through the owned `_config_sources.repo_root(explicit)` described as '(env>cwd)', but repo_root() actually resolves explicit > REBAR_ROOT > git-toplevel-of-cwd > cwd. The current completion_banking._open falls back to Path.cwd() directly (no git-toplevel step). Adopting repo_root() therefore changes the run-scoped scratch-dir base when neither explicit nor REBAR_ROOT is set, moving the bank directory to the git toplevel.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd04521d033d2dd07","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 ('reuse ... _config_sources.repo_root(explicit) (env>cwd)') / completion_banking REBAR_ROOT read","norm_id":"n8d20c0ac064e2952","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A completion-banking run with no explicit repo_root and REBAR_ROOT unset, invoked from a subdirectory of a git repo: current code uses cwd; repo_root() uses the git toplevel, relocating .rebar/workflow_runs/<run>/bank"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a narrow owned resolver mirroring the current explicit>REBAR_ROOT>Path.cwd(